            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0102" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/9–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-30T18:00:00-05:00">September 30,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Reurtel 779 September 23. Secy and Un Secy made following points re question
                    recog: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Time for decision when or if recog has not yet arrived as central Chi
                            Comm govt not yet officially established.</item>
                        <pb facs="0103" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Dept will undertake closest consultation with Cong prior taking any
                            action re recog Chi Comm regime.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Dept desires keep in close touch, and if feasible concert efforts,
                            with all concerned friendly nations on major Chi questions, including
                            problem recog.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>For urinfo only, early recog by US highly unlikely. Likewise Dept’s info
                    indicates Brit Govt will not be hasty in according recog.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
